        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(imessage): keep CLI stderr tail truncation UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`appendIMessageCliStderrTail()` in `extensions/imessage/src/cli-output.ts` uses `next.slice(-maxChars)` for tail truncation of iMessage CLI stderr output. A negative slice can split a surrogate pair at the leading edge of the tail.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced raw `.slice(-maxChars)` with `sliceUtf16Safe(next, -maxChars)` from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice`.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- iMessage CLI stderr output keeps emoji intact at the tail boundary\n- No behavior change for ASCII text\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 1 new test case in `cli-output.test.ts` — verifies emoji at tail boundary stays intact\n- Existing tests continue to pass\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
